  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origins
    
    A Nightshelf cult sworn to communion with the deep-memory of Thrall☽ Vavmastius, the volcanic forge-settlement at the Berg's core. The Communion emerged during the Clever Ice Age from the conviction that the Berg's fire-core veins held not merely heat but *memory* — that ice read under sufficient depth and blood would yield scripture. Zhachelang zhihi'Opalum, a merchant, founded the group as a deliberate challenge to the Fire Keepers' monopoly on deep-forge knowledge. That the founding impulse was commercial rather than mystical is a detail the Communion's own liturgy has quietly buried.
    
    The cult's central practice is the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, a meditation technique that fractures consciousness along aurora-lines. They have replaced their sacred focus three times. Each replacement, by all accounts, was prompted by the previous one's destruction under ritual stress. Their binding oaths fall under Pactum∴myster — blood-oath silence — while the broader creed of Mandatum∴absconditu, the law of hiddenness, has spread well beyond their membership into merchant guilds and shadow networks.
    
    ## Doctrine and the Incursion
    
    ☽'Iarlocias the Silent, a mystic and thief, and ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~, whose role the sources leave imprecise, codified The Way∴al — a doctrine that spread rapidly through Nightshelf tunnels during the Orca Incursion, when the surface-negotiated Flipper Accord appeared to many below as capitulation. The Incursion scattered the Communion's membership and inflicted losses they have not recovered from.
    
    ## The Schism
    
    The Communion fractured into two camps. Purists hold to Pactum∴myster's original vision and the deep-rites. Pragmatists have allied with the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, Aureate (the merchant guild descended from The Still Pools), and surface-aligned factions to ensure survival. Each camp considers the other's position a betrayal of everything.
    
    The split deepened after a ritual at the Bastion Apex, an ancient crystalline structure. The purists believe the ceremony woke something beneath the ice. The pragmatists maintain it did not. Neither faction has returned to verify.
    
    ## Artifacts and Custody
    
    The Communion holds several items of concern. The ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a fire-core shadow-steel blade, was lost to the orca Thung Thrakrek by theft during the Incursion. ☽'Iarlocias recovered it by theft in return. It now rests silk-wrapped under ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~'s care, bearing an irreparable fracture that widens with each use. The Thaw-Paths Medallion, an aurora-glass artifact, was kept in their inner shrine, stolen, restored, and enshrined again under Stillness-Bound protocols; priests rotate its watch in shifts no one volunteers for. They also hold ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~, seized from the ☽'shadow Covens' Order — a seizure that itself mirrors the hoarding they accuse the Fire Keepers of.
    
    ## Present Status
    
    The Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith restricts deep-tunnel access below the seventh vein of Nightfall Shelf specifically for former Communion initiates holding pre-schism knowledge of the Spiral, though neither signatory names the Communion directly. They meet in rotating caverns wearing ash-gray robes with ember-thread hems visible only in absolute darkness. Their deliberate breaking of sanctified zones continues to spread corruption through the deep ice.
